[23.121496, "o", "public: local integrity verified (T1/T2/T4); 1 tail(s); all events are signature-covered; 1 \r\nbackup key(s), which sign nothing until restored (see census — informational, not a break); \r\nexternal witness (T3): not covered — nothing outside this machine attests this record\r\n  census [backup-key] public \r\n4207f6fc361541c35c6ec921494f2be650059e41f0b5605042de9c7caae07963: the backup key this machine \r\nregistered for mnid:3561a2ee16e4e3d6ec2f6bda21bf1b0a928aae32c0929307959ef503f8b28947 — a \r\nbackup signs nothing until it is restored, so it has no tail (if it was restored and has \r\nsigned, that tail is not here)\r\nprivate: no record here — nothing has been written to this tree on this machine, so there \r\nis nothing to rule on\r\n"]
